  "configuration_id": "config_035",
  "reason": "The dominant finding so far is the massive jump from singleprofile (~0.537) to multiprofile (0.706) in config_009, but it is unclear whether this gain comes from having multiple profiles per cell or from the synergistic multimodal combination. config_035 (rna_only, multiprofile, scvi_n200, avgpool) is the cleanest single-variable comparison to config_009: it removes only the image modality while keeping the same RNA encoder and aggregation. If RNA-only multiprofile also approaches ~0.70, the gain is profile-driven and image encoders become low priority; if it drops substantially, the multimodal fusion is essential and we should focus on image encoder and fusion choices. This experiment also directly contrasts with config_023 (RNA singleprofile, 0.520) to isolate the multiprofile effect without any image confound. Under a limited budget, resolving whether the multiprofile gain is modality-independent or fusion-dependent is the highest-value uncertainty to reduce before committing further experiments to encoder or fusion variants."
}

